1343		There exists a distribution $D$
1344		over tuples $(\ell, \ell_X, \ell_Z)$, where $\ell$ is a line in
1345		$\F_q^{2m+2}$ and $\ell_X, \ell_Z$ are lines in $\F_q^m$, with the
1346		following properties:
1347		\begin{enumerate}
1348			\item The marginal distribution over $\ell$ is the same as the
1349			marginal of the line-point distribution over $\F_q^{2m+2}$.
1350			% The source phrases the next property as: the marginal over
1351			% (ell_X, ell_Z) is "a mixture of the product distributions
1352			% D_{ALine,i} x D_{ALine,j} and D_{DLine,i} x D_{DLine,j}". Those
1353			% products are distributions over pairs of line-point pairs, not
1354			% over pairs of lines, so the phrase does not define the asserted
1355			% marginal distribution on pairs of lines as written; the
1356			% formulation below states the mixture at the level of the joint
1357			% law of (ell_X, ell_Z, u), which is what the proofs of
